cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite the NuShuPARS paper."
title: "NuShuPARS: Intelligent Assisted Interpretation of Nüshu Poetry Based on Jiangyong Dialect Pronunciation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "陈"
    given-names: "灵韫"
  - family-names: "李"
    given-names: "桐"
  - family-names: "毛"
    given-names: "腾跃"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PLACEHOLDER/NuShuPARS"
abstract: >-
  NuShuPARS is a research prototype for assisted interpretation of Nüshu
  (women's script) poetry via Jiangyong dialect pronunciation: Nushu glyph
  -> dialect reading -> Hanzi candidate pool -> semantic ranking. The
  dataset in this repository is a pointer version (metadata, readings and
  SHA-256 pointers only; copyrighted translation text is not included).
keywords:
  - Nüshu
  - endangered scripts
  - Jiangyong dialect
  - low-resource NLP
  - cultural heritage
